 zero. Lower bounds may be negative (a flow against the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge, with a signed type). A self-loop carries its lower bound. When there is no such flow,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"findCirculationBarrier(supply:lowerBound:capacity:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives a set of vertices that proves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Computed by reduction to a maximum flow (push–relabel) from a super source serving each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s imbalance after the lower bounds. Which flow is returned when several exist is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n² √m)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every lower bound is at most its capacity; no value is NaN or infinite; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supplies sum to zero; the lower bounds and supplies at a vertex sum without overflow, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"capacity − lower bound does not overflow."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"Flows","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows","url":"\/documentation\/flows"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedGraph","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/Directed